      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "POMAH (2) resumed in top order when winning fresh up on a heavy track at Geelong just over 3 weeks ago. She is bred to excel over more ground, so the extra 225m won't be any bother, and in a field that is not much tougher, she can repeat the dose, especially if the track is wet again. OF THE VIEW (5) stuck on gamely as the favourite at Echuca 8-days ago when finishing second by a head after sharing the pace throughout. She has a handy gate and could take some pegging back here. Follow your money. REAL ALLIANCE (1) has been down on her best and will drop further in class for this. We are prepared to give her another chance in this company. Keep her very safe. QUEEN AMANJENA (7) was less than a length from the winner when finishing fourth last start, and she has top 4 claims again.",
